{{!-- What a signed-in Member sees where the sign-in or sign-up card would be.

	{{> "auth/signed-in" cardTitle=(t "You are signed in")}}      from inside auth/shell.hbs

	cardTitle   the heading, which differs by Surface. Not `title`: the shell passes its own hash
	            down with the context, and `title` there is the page's h1

A form that would create a second account for someone who already has one is worse than no form.
The address is `{{@member.email}}`, which is Ghost's own answer to "who is this", and the action
is Portal's account panel — the one members screen a theme genuinely cannot template and should
not try to. --}}
<div class="text-center">
	<h2 class="font-display tracking-heading text-2xl leading-[1.2] font-medium">{{cardTitle}}</h2>

	<p class="text-small text-muted mt-3.5 leading-[1.65]">{{@member.email}}</p>

	<a
		href="#/portal/account"
		data-portal="account"
		class="btn btn-primary font-ui mt-[26px] inline-block rounded-sm border px-5 py-[11px] text-sm font-semibold no-underline">{{t "Manage your account"}}</a>
</div>
